@startuml STM-2
!include _style.iuml
title STM-2 (System level) — Status of a Connector\nconnectors.status · v1.0 · 01/11/2026

[*] -down-> Unavailable
note left of Unavailable
  created when the Operator
  onboards the Charge Point (AD-8)
end note

state Operational {
  [*] -down-> Available
  state "Energy transfer" as ET {
    [*] -down-> Charging
    Charging -left-> SuspendedEV : vehicle pauses
    SuspendedEV -right-> Charging : vehicle resumes
    Charging -right-> SuspendedEVSE : Charge Point pauses
    SuspendedEVSE -left-> Charging : Charge Point resumes
  }
  Available -down-> Preparing : Driver authorized\nor plugs in
  Preparing -up-> Available : authorization refused\nor plug-in timeout
  Preparing -down-> ET : charging starts
  ET -down-> Finishing : charging stops
  Finishing -up-> Available : Driver unplugs
  Available -right-> Reserved : Charge Point holds it\nfor a reservation
  Reserved -left-> Available : hold released
  Reserved -down-> Preparing : reserving Driver\nauthorized
}

Unavailable -right-> Operational : Charge Point reports it ready\n(after connecting or back in service)
Operational -left-> Unavailable : taken out of service\nor Charge Point restarts
Operational -down-> Faulted : fault reported\n/ hide from search
Faulted -up-> Operational : fault cleared\n/ show in search
Faulted -left-> Unavailable : Charge Point restarts\nor taken out of service

note right of Operational
  The Charge Point owns these states;
  the platform records each report.
  A report outside these transitions is
  still recorded and flagged, never refused.
  Reserved only with reservations (Should).
  "Offline" is not a connector status: it
  comes from the Charge Point connection
  (STM-3). Operational and Energy transfer
  group states; they are not status values.
end note
@enduml
